IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ks-types`
IMPORT `ks-membership`
IMPORT `ks-contributions`
IMPORT `ks-withdrawals`

-- KiwiSaver Act 2006 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For this person and this employment, does automatic enrolment apply and
--    until when may they opt out; what must be deducted from this pay and
--    what must the employer contribute; and how much may they withdraw for
--    the purpose they give?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `KiwiSaver case` HAS
    `the person`                                        IS A Person
    `the employment`                                    IS AN Employment
    `the pay`                                           IS A `Contribution facts`
    `the employer's side`                               IS AN `Employer contribution facts`
    `the withdrawal sought`                             IS A MAYBE `Withdrawal facts`
    `the account`                                       IS A `Member account`

DECLARE `KiwiSaver position` HAS
    `automatic enrolment applies`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `first day to opt out`                              IS A MAYBE DATE
    `last day to opt out`                               IS A MAYBE DATE
    `contribution rate`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `deduction from the pay`                            IS A NUMBER
    `compulsory employer contribution`                  IS A NUMBER
    `most that may be withdrawn`                        IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref ss 6, 10-21, 62-66, 101A-101FC; Schedule 1 cls 4-14C
@export default The KiwiSaver position under the KiwiSaver Act 2006 (NZ) for one person, one employment and one pay: whether automatic enrolment applies and the opt-out window (the 13th to the 55th day after starting); the contribution rate and the deduction from the pay (none during a savings suspension or a non-deduction notice); the compulsory employer contribution; and, if a withdrawal is sought, the most that may be withdrawn for its purpose under the scheme rules. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `KiwiSaver case`  @desc The person (birth date, qualification age, residence, membership), the employment (start, kind, exemptions), the pay (rate history, chosen rate, rate reduction, suspension, date, gross amount), the employer's side (s 101C facts, other contributions, grace period), any withdrawal sought, and the member's account
GIVETH A `KiwiSaver position`
`the KiwiSaver position for` c MEANS
    `KiwiSaver position` WITH
        `automatic enrolment applies`                   IS enrolled
        `first day to opt out`                          IS IF enrolled THEN JUST (`the first day to opt out, employment started` started) ELSE NOTHING
        `last day to opt out`                           IS IF enrolled THEN JUST (`the last day to opt out, employment started` started) ELSE NOTHING
        `contribution rate`                             IS `the contribution rate for` (c's `the pay`)
        `deduction from the pay`                        IS `the deduction from the pay` (c's `the pay`)
        `compulsory employer contribution`              IS `the compulsory employer contribution for` (c's `the pay`) `and` (c's `the employer's side`)
        `most that may be withdrawn`                    IS
            CONSIDER c's `the withdrawal sought`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST w THEN JUST (`the most the member may withdraw, facts` w `, account` (c's `the account`))
    WHERE
        enrolled MEANS `automatic enrolment applies to` (c's `the person`) `, employment` (c's `the employment`)
        started  MEANS `the day the new employment starts for` (c's `the employment`)
